Project Title

Population Group-wise Deposits Analysis Using Python

Description

This project analyzes population group-wise bank deposits across various states, districts, and regions in India using Python. The analysis focuses on understanding deposit distributions, account numbers, and banking office availability across Rural, Semi-Urban, Urban, and Metropolitan regions. The project includes data cleaning, handling missing values, exploratory data analysis, statistical summaries, and visualizations such as bar charts, pie charts, and line plots. The insights generated help understand banking penetration and deposit distribution trends across different population groups.
Getting Started

Dependencies

•	Python 3.x
•	Google Colab or Jupyter Notebook
•	Windows 10/11, Linux, or macOS
•	pandas
•	numpy
•	matplotlib
•	IPython

Installing

•	Download or clone the repository from GitHub:
git clone https://github.com/kalaiavk1516-create/Data_Analytics_final_project.git
•	Navigate to the project folder:
cd Data_Analytics_final_project
•	Install the required Python libraries:
pip install pandas numpy matplotlib ipython


Executing program


•	Open the notebook in Google Colab or Jupyter Notebook.
•	Load the dataset.
•	Clean and preprocess the data.
•	Perform exploratory data analysis.
•	Generate visualizations and insights.

import pandas as pd

df = pd.read_csv(
    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kalaiavk1516-create/Data_Analytics_final_project/refs/heads/main/populationgroup-wise-deposits.csv"
)

display(df.head())


